.TH VOCK 1 "August 2026" "vock 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vock \- map a userspace program to the kernel code it exercises
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vock
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIargs\fR...]
.br
.B vock
\fIsubcommand\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vock
runs
.I command
and reports which kernel source lines it caused to execute, as an annotated
HTML or terminal report.
.PP
Coverage comes from one of two sources. KCOV
.RB ( \-\-mode
.BR kcov )
needs a kernel built with
.BR CONFIG_KCOV ,
and collects per-thread coverage through an LD_PRELOAD shim that follows
.BR fork (2),
.BR vfork (2)
and
.BR pthread_create (3).
Hardware trace
.RB ( \-\-mode
.BR hw )
needs no kernel instrumentation and uses Intel Processor Trace or AMD LBR on
x86-64, or CoreSight ETM on arm64.
kcov-dataflow
.RB ( \-\-mode
.BR dataflow )
needs a kernel built with
.BR CONFIG_KCOV_DATAFLOW_ARGS " and " CONFIG_KCOV_DATAFLOW_RET
(the kcov-dataflow clang) and records, for the traced task, every
instrumented function's arguments and return value in execution order,
written as
.IR dataflow.log ", " dataflow.txt " and " dataflow.html
next to the usual coverage report.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-mode " " \fIkcov\fR|\fIhw\fR|\fIdataflow\fR
Coverage source. Default is hardware trace when available.
.TP
.BR \-\-remote\-handle " " \fIH\fR
With
.BR \-\-mode " " dataflow ,
also publish a buffer for kernel code that brackets its work with
.BR kcov_df_remote_start (\fIH\fR),
written to
.IR dataflow-remote.log .
.TP
.BR \-\-vmlinux " " \fIPATH\fR
Uninstrumented vmlinux with debug info, used to resolve addresses.
.TP
.BR \-\-kernel\-src " " \fIPATH\fR
Kernel source tree, used to quote source lines in the report.
.TP
.B \-\-btf
Resolve symbols through BTF and kallsyms instead of DWARF.
.TP
.BR \-\-filter " " \fIKEYWORD\fR
Restrict the report to paths matching \fIKEYWORD\fR, e.g. \fBfs\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-ordered
Emit one report per thread, \fIcoverage-<TID>.html\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-syscall " " \fIptrace\fR|\fIsud\fR|\fIebpf\fR
Backend used to trace the target's syscalls.
.TP
.B \-\-syzlang
Also write the trace as a syzkaller program, \fItrace.syz\fR.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B report
Regenerate a report from an existing coverage log.
.TP
.B execprog
Replay a syzkaller program, including an unmodified syzbot reproducer, or a
plain syscall trace. Supports per-call coverage with \fB\-cover\fR.
.TP
.B prog2c
Convert a syscall trace into a standalone C reproducer.
.TP
.B fuzz
Trace a command, then re-execute the resulting program repeatedly.
.TP
.B selftest
Build a suitable kernel and exercise each mode. Requires a kernel source tree
and \fBvirtme-ng\fR; intended for development rather than installed use.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/vock/kcov.so
The LD_PRELOAD coverage shim. Override its location with
.BR VOCK_KCOV_SO .
.TP
.I kerncov.log
Kernel program counters from the run, written to the current directory.
.TP
.I coverage.html
The generated report.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VOCK_KCOV_SO
Path to the coverage shim, overriding the built-in search.
.TP
.B VOCK_ADDR2LINE
External addr2line-compatible tool (GNU or LLVM) to symbolize with, instead
of the built-in in-process DWARF reader. Also used as the fallback when the
vmlinux cannot be read in-process.
.TP
.B VOCK_NO_PREWARM
Do not load the vmlinux DWARF on a background thread while the target runs.
.TP
.B VOCK_DWARF_FULL_INDEX
Index compilation units from every unit header instead of .debug_aranges
(automatic when the vmlinux has no .debug_aranges, as with LLVM=1 builds).
.TP
.B VOCK_PREFETCH_THREADS
Threads used to prefetch vmlinux pages before parsing (default 8, 0 disables).
.TP
.B VOCK_TIMING
Print a wall-clock mark on stderr at every stage of a run (\fB1\fP), or
append the marks to the named file.
.TP
.B VOCK_PROG_INT_WIDTH
Width in bytes assumed for an integer inside a compound argument when
replaying a syzkaller program. Default 8.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns the traced command's exit status, or 1 on setup failure.
.SH NOTES
.B \-\-mode
.B kcov
requires root and a kernel with
.BR CONFIG_KCOV .
.B \-\-mode
.B hw
requires
.I /proc/sys/kernel/perf_event_paranoid
to be 1 or less, or root.
.B \-\-mode
.B dataflow
requires root and a kernel with
.BR CONFIG_KCOV_DATAFLOW_ARGS / RET ;
see
.I /usr/share/doc/vock/DATAFLOW.md.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR perf (1),
.BR strace (1),
.BR llvm-addr2line (1),
.BR addr2line (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Yunseong Kim <yunseong.kim@est.tech>
